cs","concept.combinatorics.idea":"Clever counting: combinations, stars and bars, the pigeonhole principle and inclusion–exclusion.","concept.combinatorics.seen":"Estimating search spaces, hashing collisions, probability, puzzle interviews","reveal.combinatorics":"Counted without listing a single case.","place.dynamic_programming.name":"Dynamic programming","place.dynamic_programming.tagline":"Solve small cases, reuse them","scene.dynamic_programming.stairs.objective":"You climb {n} stairs, taking this many steps at a time. In how many different ways can you reach the top?","scene.dynamic_programming.coins.objective":"Using these coins as often as you like, what is the fewest coins that make {amount}?","scene.dynamic_programming.grid_paths.objective":"Move only right or down, avoiding ■. How many paths go from the top-left to the bottom-right?","hint.dynamic_programming.1":"Answer the small cases first: 1 stair, 2 stairs, an amount of 1, the first row.","hint.dynamic_programming.2":"Each answer is built from answers you already have.","hint.dynamic_programming.3":"Stairs: add the ways from the steps below. Coins: 1 + the best for the amount minus each coin. Grid: add the cell above and the cell to the left.","concept.dynamic_programming.name":"Dynamic programming","concept.dynamic_programming.idea":"Store the answers to small cases and build bigger answers from them, so nothing is worked out twice.","concept.dynamic_programming.seen":"Edit distance, route planning, coin change, many interview problems","reveal.dynamic_programming":"You reused small answers to build the big one.","place.knapsack.name":"Knapsack","place.knapsack.tagline":"Best value within a limit","scene.knapsack.bag.objective":"Fill the bag up to {cap} kg with the highest total value.","hint.knapsack.1":"The most valuable items are not always the best choice.","hint.knapsack.2":"Look at value per kilogram, but check that the leftover space is not wasted.","hint.knapsack.3":"Try swapping one item for 