 answer","place.search_the_answer.tagline":"Binary search on the result","scene.search_the_answer.ship.objective":"Ship these parcels in this order within {days} days. What is the smallest daily limit that works?","scene.search_the_answer.isqrt.objective":"What is the biggest whole number whose square is at most {n}?","hint.search_the_answer.1":"Guess an answer and check whether it works.","hint.search_the_answer.2":"If a limit works, every bigger limit works too, so binary search the answer.","hint.search_the_answer.3":"The answer is at least the heaviest parcel and at most the total weight.","concept.search_the_answer.name":"Binary search on the answer","concept.search_the_answer.idea":"When bigger answers keep working once one does, you can binary search the answer itself.","concept.search_the_answer.seen":"Capacity planning, square roots, splitting work evenly, many interview problems","reveal.search_the_answer":"You searched the answer, not the data.","place.xor_tricks.name":"XOR tricks","place.xor_tricks.tagline":"Things that cancel out","scene.xor_tricks.subset.objective":"Pick tiles whose XOR is {target}.","scene.xor_tricks.single.objective":"Every number appears twice except one. Which one is alone?","scene.xor_tricks.swap.objective":"Run the three lines. What are a and b at the end?","hint.xor_tricks.1":"x ^ x = 0 and x ^ 0 = x.","hint.xor_tricks.2":"XOR is about bits: a column ends up 1 when an odd number of the picked tiles have a 1 there.","hint.xor_tricks.3":"Pairs cancel each other out, so XOR of everything leaves the lone number.","concept.xor_tricks.name":"XOR","concept.xor_tricks.idea":"XOR cancels pairs: x ^ x = 0. That finds lone items, swaps values and checks parity.","concept.xor_tricks.seen":"Finding the single number, RAID parity, checksums, simple encryption","reveal.xor_tricks":"The pairs cancelled out.","place.union_find.name":"Union–find","place.union_find.tagline":"Who is connected to whom","scene.union_find.groups.objective":"People 1 to {n}. Each link joins two people into the same group. How many groups are there?","scene.union_find.groups_biggest.objective":"People 1 to {n}. Each link joins two groups. How many groups are there, and how big is the biggest?","hint.union_find.1":"Start with everyone in their own group.","hint.union_find.2":"Each link merges two groups, unless they are already the same group.","hint.union_find.3":"People with no links are groups of one.","concept.union_find.name":"Union–find","concept.union_find.idea":"Track groups by merging them as links arrive, without redrawing the whole picture.","concept.union_find.seen":"Network connectivity, Kruskal’s spanning trees, friend circles, image regions","reveal.union_find":"You merged the groups as the links came in.","place.probability.name":"Probability","place.probability.tagline":"Count the outcomes","scene.probability.dice_sum.objective":"You roll two dice. In how many of the 36 outcomes is the total {s}?","scene.probability.heads.objective":"You flip {n} coins. How many outcomes have exactly {k} heads?","scene.probability.at_least_one_six.objective":"You roll {n} dice. How many outcomes have at least one six?","hint.probability.1":"List the ways in a small table, or count them.","hint.probability.2":"Exactly k heads: choose which k coins are heads, C(n, k).","hint.probability.3":"At least one: count all outcomes, then take away the ones with none.","concept.probability.name":"Counting outcomes","concept.probability.idea":"Probability is favourable outcomes divided by all outcomes, so count carefully.","concept.probability.seen":"Randomised algorithms, testing, load estimates, hash collisions","reveal.probability":"Counted every outcome that counts.","place.caching.name":"Caching","place.caching.tagline":"What to keep, what to drop","scene.caching.lru.objective":"A cache holds {cap} items and drops the least recently used. How many requests are misses?","scene.caching.fifo.objective":"A cache holds {cap} items and drops the oldest one added. How many requests are misses?","hint.caching.1":"A miss is a request for something not in the cache. Then it gets added.","hint.caching.2":"When the cache is full, one item has to go first.","hint.caching.3":"LRU: a hit makes an item fresh again. FIFO: hits change nothing.","concept.caching.name":"Caching","concept.caching.idea":"A cache keeps recent items close. The eviction rule decides how often you miss.","concept.caching.seen":"CPU caches, browser caches, CDNs, database buffers","reveal.caching":"You kept the right things in the cache.","place.rate_limiting.name":"Load and limits","place.rate_limiting.tagline":"Rate limits and load balancing","scene.rate_limiting.token_bucket.objective":"The bucket holds {cap} tokens, starts full and gains {rate} each second. Each request uses one. Requests per second are shown. How many get through?","scene.rate_limiting.round_robin.objective":"{m} servers take requests in turn, starting with server 1. Which server gets request {n}?","scene.rate_limiting.least_loaded.objective":"Each job goes to whichever of the {servers} servers has the least work so far. How much work does the busiest server end up with?","hint.rate_limiting.1":"Simulate it one second, or one job, at a time.","hint.rate_limiting.2":"Round robin is a remainder: work out which turn of the cycle you are on.","hint.rate_limiting.3":"Token bucket: requests beyond the tokens left are refused, and the bucket never holds more than its size.","concept.rate_limiting.name":"Rate limiting and load balancing","concept.rate_limiting.idea":"Token buckets smooth out bursts; round robin and least-loaded spread work across servers.","concept.rate_limiting.seen":"API gateways, web servers, queues, cloud autoscaling","reveal.rate_limiting":"Traffic shared out fairly.","tier.easy":"Easy","tier.medium":"Medium","tier.hard":"Hard","action.answer":"Check","action.probe":"Check","action.pick":"Check","action.ops":"Check","action.route":"Check","tip.answer":"Tap a field, then enter your answer.","tip.probe":"Drag along the line or use − and +, then check.","tip.pick":"Tap tiles to pick them.","tip.ops":"Make your moves, then check.","tip.route":"Drag from the orange dot to the ring.","ok.answer":"Correct.","ok.probe":"Pinned down.","ok.pick":"That works.","ok.ops":"That works.","ok.route":"No path does better.","fail.answer.empty":"Fill in every answer first.","fail.answer.wrong":"Not quite.","fail.answer.some_wrong":"Some answers are off.","fail.probe.out_of_checks":"Out of checks with more than one number left.","fail.pick.empty":"Pick some tiles first.","fail.pick.wrong_count":"That is not the right number of tiles.","fail.pick.too_much":"That adds up to too much.","fail.pick.too_little":"That adds up to too little.","fail.pick.wrong_xor":"Those tiles XOR to a different number.","fail.pick.not_together":"A window has to be tiles next to each other.","fail.pick.not_best":"That works, but a better choice exists.","fail.pick.overlap":"Two of those overlap.","fail.pick.over_cap":"Too heavy for the bag.","fail.ops.wrong_order":"Something came out in the wrong order.","fail.ops.unfinished":"Not finished yet.","fail.ops.unsorted":"Not in order yet.","fail.ops.too_many_moves":"Sorted, but with more swaps than needed.","fail.ops.too_early":"A task came before something it needs.","fail.route.unfinished":"The path has to reach the ring.","fail.route.longer":"That gets there, but a better path exists.","probe.higher":"higher","probe.lower":"lower","probe.good":"good","probe.bad":"bad","probe.found":"found","probe.start":"Pick a number to check.","probe.left":"{left} still possible.","probe.bisect_note":"Bad means the first bad one is here or earlier.","ops.push":"Push","ops.pop":"Pop","ops.target":"Target","ops.in":"In","ops.out":"Out","route.steps":"Steps","route.cost":"Cost","field.front":"Front","field.size":"Size","field.last_out":"Last out","field.first_out":"First out","field.top":"Top","field.groups":"Groups","field.biggest":"Biggest","ui.locked_tier":"Solve {count} more {tier} scenes to open this topic."}
